    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0735" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Wendelin, Eric C./86: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Straus</hi>)<anchor n="57" xml:id="d590-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-23T16:00:00-04:00">July 23, 1936—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. Please convey following to Wendelin, Madrid: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Department highly gratified at the timeliness and thoroughness of your
                            reports and steps you are taking to protect Americans in Madrid. You are
                            authorized to draw for such reasonable funds as are necessary to
                            purchase food, employ guards and provide any other equipment which you
                            may require in connection with the care of American citizens and
                            protection of Embassy.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d590-f1" n="57" type="source" xml:id="d590-f1-content">
                <p>A somewhat similar telegram (No. 242, July 23, 3 p.m.) was sent to the Ambassador
                    in France for the Consul at Barcelona.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
